Text Analyzer – Python Package

A simple Python text analysis project that demonstrates packages, modules, imports, and code reusability. It cleans text and generates a report containing the total number of words, characters, and vowels.

Features
Converts text to lowercase.
Normalizes whitespace by removing extra spaces, tabs, and newlines.
Counts the total number of words.
Counts characters, including single spaces between words.
Counts vowels (a, e, i, o, u).
Generates a formatted text analysis report.
Uses a Python package to organize code into separate modules.
Uses a main guard to prevent input prompts from running during imports.
Project Structure
text_analyzer/
├── main.py
├── analyzer/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── cleaning.py
│   ├── metrics.py
│   └── report.py
└── README.md
Technologies Used
Python
Python Modules and Packages
Functions and Imports
How It Works
The user enters a text string in main.py.
cleaning.py converts the text to lowercase and normalizes whitespace.
metrics.py calculates the word count, character count, and vowel count.
report.py combines the results into a formatted report.
__init__.py exposes the selected functions for convenient importing.
How to Run

Step 1: Open the terminal in the project directory.

Step 2: Run the following command:

python main.py

Step 3: Enter your text when prompted.

Example

Input:

pYTHon IS fuN

Output:

----------------text report--------------------------
cleaned text: python is fun
total words: 3
total characters: 13
total vowels: 3
Concepts Demonstrated
Python packages and modules
The __init__.py file
